Subject: [PATCH] hwsim: preserve per-BSS management receive context

The HAL subscribes to management frames separately for each AP interface.
mac80211 therefore reports broadcast probe requests once per receiving BSS.
The hostapd event currently omits rx_mgmt.drv_priv, so hostapd_mgmt_rx fans
each notification out to every BSS on that radio again. Three listening
BSSes generate three responses per advertised BSSID for one probe request.
During concurrent client scans this multiplies medium queues and delays
native authentication responses beyond their receive deadline.

Set the existing per-BSS driver identity for both normal and explicitly
forwarded AP events. Preserve receive frequency and signal in the normal
nl80211 path. This uses hostapd's existing per-BSS dispatch contract, without
deduplicating packets by time, dropping legitimate probes, reprioritizing
management subtypes or changing authentication/steering timers. Scope the
adaptation to HWSIM_RADIO; physical-driver and STA dispatch remain unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
+++ b/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
@@ -2496,6 +2496,10 @@
         os_memset(&event, 0, sizeof(event));
         event.rx_mgmt.frame = (unsigned char *)mgmt;
         event.rx_mgmt.frame_len = len;
+#ifdef HWSIM_RADIO
+        event.rx_mgmt.freq = recv_freq;
+        event.rx_mgmt.ssi_signal = sig_dbm;
+#endif
 #ifdef CMXB7_PORT
         event.rx_mgmt.snr_db = snr;
 #endif
@@ -2512,6 +2516,9 @@
             supplicant_event(&interface->wpa_s, EVENT_RX_MGMT, &event);
 #endif
         } else {
+#ifdef HWSIM_RADIO
+            event.rx_mgmt.drv_priv = interface->u.ap.hapd.drv_priv;
+#endif
             wpa_supplicant_event(&interface->u.ap.hapd, EVENT_RX_MGMT, &event);
         }
         pthread_mutex_unlock(&g_wifi_hal.hapd_lock);
@@ -14321,6 +14328,9 @@
         supplicant_event(&interface->wpa_s, EVENT_RX_MGMT, &event);
 #endif
     } else {
+#ifdef HWSIM_RADIO
+        event.rx_mgmt.drv_priv = interface->u.ap.hapd.drv_priv;
+#endif
         wpa_supplicant_event(&interface->u.ap.hapd, EVENT_RX_MGMT, &event);
     }
     pthread_mutex_unlock(&g_wifi_hal.hapd_lock);
